      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RAYMAR FOX (1) had the drop on the lead and went on to be beaten 2.25 lengths into second (22.03) at this track in a Grade 4 over 380m. Solid formlines coming through his last run. Racing well and deserves a win. SUNSET BOY (2) is a capable type and proved too classy last time to win by 6 lengths at this track in a handy 22.22 beating Mizuki Magic. One of main contenders. FEDERAL GALAXY (6) goes very well at the course and distance with two wins and a placing from five starts. Was out of the placings last time (22.28) at this track in a Grade 5, finishing fifth and beaten 7 lengths. Suited here and expected to run well. RACCOON ROGER (4) is worth some thought after being close-up last start.",
